sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Consumer as SDK Consumer
    participant Config as CKKSConfig
    participant Session as HESession
    participant Adapter as Backend Adapter
    participant Native as Native HE Runtime
    participant Workspace as Encrypted Workspace
    actor Recipient as Result Recipient

    Consumer->>Config: profile("ckks-balanced-v1")
    Config-->>Consumer: immutable CKKSConfig
    Consumer->>Session: create(device, config)
    Session->>Adapter: select and create one backend
    Adapter->>Native: create context and key bundle
    Native-->>Session: context, public/secret/evaluation keys
    Session-->>Consumer: trusted HESession

    Consumer->>Session: encrypt(values)
    Session->>Native: encode and encrypt
    Native-->>Session: ciphertext handle
    Session-->>Consumer: EncryptedVector + metadata

    Consumer->>Session: HE calculation
    Note over Consumer,Session: add · subtract · multiply · square<br/>sum · mean · variance
    Session->>Session: validate ownership, compatibility and depth
    Session->>Adapter: dispatch selected operation
    Adapter->>Native: execute on ciphertext
    Native-->>Session: encrypted result
    Session-->>Consumer: EncryptedVector or EncryptedScalar

    opt Persist encrypted data on CPU
        Consumer->>Session: save(value, workspace, name)
        Session->>Workspace: public material + ciphertext + metadata
        Workspace-->>Session: artifact path
        Session-->>Consumer: artifact path
    end

    alt Trusted owner decrypts
        Consumer->>Session: decrypt(result)
        Session->>Native: decrypt with owner secret key
        Native-->>Consumer: plaintext value(s)
    else CPU aggregate is released to recipient
        Recipient-->>Session: recipient public key
        Consumer->>Session: release_result(sum/mean/variance, recipient)
        Session->>Native: proxy re-encrypt aggregate
        Native-->>Recipient: ReleasedResult ciphertext
        Recipient->>Recipient: decrypt with recipient secret key
    end

    Consumer->>Session: close()
    Session->>Adapter: close backend
    Adapter->>Native: release native resources
    Session-->>Consumer: None

    Note over Session,Native: CPU and GPU are separate native runtimes.<br/>There is no automatic fallback between them.
